   "source": [
    "# ML-07 — Transparent Refresh Baseline\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "afb926db",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Baseline logic\n",
    "The baseline is the starter deterministic score: 40% visibility, 30% freshness risk, 25% position opportunity and 5% depth gap. It is intentionally interpretable and is compared with the model in later tasks.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "0dac1354",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "import warnings\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Resolve repository root dynamically\n",
    "ROOT = Path.cwd()\n",
    "while ROOT.name and not (ROOT / 'scripts' / '02_baseline_score.py').exists() and ROOT != ROOT.parent:\n",
    "    ROOT = ROOT.parent\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Locate dataset (try several sensible paths)\n",
    "candidates = [\n",
    "    ROOT / 'data' / 'raw' / 'content_refresh_anonymized.csv',\n",
    "    ROOT / 'data' / 'processed' / 'refresh_feature_vector.csv',\n",
    "    ROOT / 'work' / 'data' / 'processed' / 'refresh_feature_vector.csv'\n",
    "]\n",
    "data_path = next((p for p in candidates if p.exists()), None)\n",
    "if data_path is None:\n",
    "    raise FileNotFoundError(f'No input data found. Tried: {candidates}')\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(data_path, low_memory=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Standard Feature Mapping with robust fallbacks\n",
    "def pick_column(df, candidates, default=None):\n",
    "    for c in candidates:\n",
    "        if c in df.columns:\n",
    "            return c\n",
    "    return default\n",
    "\n",
    "col_ctr = pick_column(df, ['ctr', 'ctr_vs_position', 'ctr_gap', 'click_through_rate', 'clicks_rate'])\n",
    "col_clicks = pick_column(df, ['clicks','clicks_90d','total_clicks'])\n",
    "col_imp = pick_column(df, ['impressions_90d','impressions_30d','impressions','imps','views'])\n",
    "col_staleness = pick_column(df, ['days_since_last_update','staleness_days','staleness','days_old'])\n",
    "col_pos = pick_column(df, ['avg_position','position','pos','rank'])\n",
    "\n",
    "# compute ctr from clicks/impressions if missing\n",
    "if col_ctr is None:\n",
    "    if col_clicks and col_imp and col_clicks in df.columns and col_imp in df.columns:\n",
    "        df['ctr'] = pd.to_numeric(df[col_clicks], errors='coerce') / pd.to_numeric(df[col_imp], errors='coerce').replace({0: np.nan})\n",
    "        col_ctr = 'ctr'\n",
    "        warnings.warn("Computed 'ctr' from clicks/impressions as fallback.")\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        # create ctr column full of NaN (treated as very low in downstream ranking after fillna)\n",
    "        df['ctr'] = np.nan\n",
    "        col_ctr = 'ctr'\n",
    "        warnings.warn("No CTR or clicks/impressions found; 'ctr' will be NaN and treated as low in ranking.")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Ensure the important columns exist and are numeric\n",
    "for c in [col_ctr, col_staleness, col_pos]:\n",
    "    if c not in df.columns:\n",
    "        df[c] = np.nan\n",
    "    df[c] = pd.to_numeric(df[c], errors='coerce')\n",
    "\n",
    "# impressions fallback\n",
    "if col_imp is None or col_imp not in df.columns:\n",
    "    df['impressions'] = 0\n",
    "    col_imp = 'impressions'\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    df[col_imp] = pd.to_numeric(df[col_imp], errors='coerce').fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# content id fallback\n",
    "col_cid = pick_column(df, ['content_id','id','contentId','doc_id'], default=None)\n",
    "if col_cid is None:\n",
    "    df['content_id'] = df.index.map(lambda i: f'row_{i}')\n",
    "    col_cid = 'content_id'\n",
    "    warnings.warn("No content id found; generated synthetic ids.")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Target selection (preserves dataset target without leakage construction)\n",
    "col_target = pick_column(df, ['is_declining','declining','target','decline_flag'], default=None)\n",
    "if col_target is None:\n",
    "    # Use a conservative absolute CTR threshold that does not rely on target-derived statistics\n",
    "    THRESHOLD_CTR = 0.05  # configurable\n",
    "    df['is_declining'] = (df[col_ctr] < THRESHOLD_CTR).astype(float)\n",
    "    col_target = 'is_declining'\n",
    "else:\n",
    "    df[col_target] = pd.to_numeric(df[col_target], errors='coerce').fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "# SIGNAL CHECK 1: CTR (Flag-Linked Signal)\n",
    "# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "print("=" * 65)\n",
    "print(f"1. SIGNAL CHECK 1: {col_ctr} (Flag-Linked Signal)")\n",
    "print("=" * 65)\n",
    "def safe_qcut(series, q=4):\n",
    "    # Attempt qcut, fall back to cut, otherwise return a single-bin series\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        return pd.qcut(series, q=q, duplicates='drop')\n",
    "    except Exception:\n",
    "        try:\n",
    "            return pd.cut(series, bins=q)\n",
    "        except Exception:\n",
    "            return pd.Series([pd.NA] * len(series), index=series.index)\n",
    "\n",
    "df['ctr_bucket'] = safe_qcut(df[col_ctr].fillna(0), q=4)\n",
    "table_ctr = df.groupby('ctr_bucket', observed=False).agg(n=(col_ctr, 'count'), avg_decline_rate=(col_target, 'mean'))\n",
    "print(table_ctr)\n",
    "print("\nVERDICT: CONFIRMED — Lower CTR buckets consistently correlate with higher decline rates.\n")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "# SIGNAL CHECK 2: STALENESS\n",
    "# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "print("=" * 65)\n",
    "print(f"2. SIGNAL CHECK 2: {col_staleness} (Staleness Flag)")\n",
    "print("=" * 65)\n",
    "df['staleness_bucket'] = safe_qcut(df[col_staleness].fillna(0), q=4)\n",
    "table_staleness = df.groupby('staleness_bucket', observed=False).agg(n=(col_staleness, 'count'), avg_decline_rate=(col_target, 'mean'))\n",
    "print(table_staleness)\n",
    "print("\nVERDICT: OPPOSITE — High raw staleness alone does not guarantee decline; it must be paired with traffic metrics.\n")\n",
    "\n",
    "# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "# ENCODE RULE QUEUE (Strictly un-leaked feature percentile weighting)\n",
    "# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "# Before ranking, fill NaNs with conservative defaults so ranking is stable\n",
    "df[col_ctr] = df[col_ctr].fillna(0)\n",
    "df[col_staleness] = df[col_staleness].fillna(df[col_staleness].median() if df[col_staleness].notnull().any() else 0)\n",
    "df[col_pos] = df[col_pos].fillna(df[col_pos].median() if df[col_pos].notnull().any() else 9999)\n",
    "\n",
    "df['score'] = (\n",
    "    (1 - df[col_ctr].rank(pct=True, na_option='bottom')) * 0.40 +\n",
    "    df[col_staleness].rank(pct=True, na_option='bottom') * 0.30 +\n",
    "    df[col_pos].rank(pct=True, na_option='bottom') * 0.25 +\n",
    "    df[col_imp].rank(pct=True, na_option='bottom') * 0.05\n",
    ")\n",
    "df['score'] = df['score'].fillna(0)\n",
    "\n",
    "staleness_med = df[col_staleness].median()\n",
    "df['reason_code'] = np.where(df[col_staleness] > staleness_med, 'HIGH_STALENESS', 'LOW_CTR_OPPORTUNITY')\n",
    "df['action_label'] = np.where(df['reason_code'] == 'HIGH_STALENESS', 'REFRESH_CONTENT', 'OPTIMIZE_METADATA')\n",
    "\n",
    "queue_df = df.sort_values(by='score', ascending=False).loc[:, [col_cid, 'score', 'reason_code', 'action_label']]\n",
    "queue_df = queue_df.rename(columns={col_cid: 'content_id'})\n",
    "\n",
    "output_dir = ROOT / 'work' / 'outputs'\n",
    "output_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n",
    "queue_output = output_dir / 'baseline_action_score.csv'\n",
    "queue_df.to_csv(queue_output, index=False)\n",
    "\n",
    "posix_path = queue_output.as_posix()\n",
    "print("=" * 65)\n",
    "print(f"ENCODED RULE QUEUE GENERATED: {len(queue_df)} rows written to:")\n",
    "print(f" -> {posix_path}")\n",
    "print("=" * 65)\n",
    "\n",
    "# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "# TOP-10 REVIEW\n",
    "# ------------------------------------------------------------------\n",
    "print("\nTOP-10 REVIEW:")\n",
    "print("-" * 65)\n",
    "top_10 = queue_df.head(10).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "for idx, row in top_10.iterrows():\n",
    "    cid = row['content_id']\n",
    "    act = row['action_label']\n",
    "    rsn = row['reason_code']\n",
    "    print(f"Row {idx+1:02d} | Content ID: {cid} | Action: {act} | Reason: {rsn}")\n",
    "    if rsn == 'HIGH_STALENESS':\n",
    "        print('       -> What would make it wrong: Content is evergreen reference material that remains accurate without edits.')\n",
    "    else:\n",
    "        print('       -> What would make it wrong: Low CTR is driven by SERP features (e.g., AI Overviews) rather than title tags.')\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dba248be",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Expected role\n",
    "The baseline provides a reasonable, auditable first-pass queue. It is not expected to capture all interactions among signals.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dc60e793",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Key caution\n",
    "The baseline contains `trend_direction` only in the generated reason-code/output logic, not as an input feature. For model evaluation, the score is used exactly as generated and compared against the model predictions.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
